    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12-a1">

                <pb facs="0132" n="16" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg16"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry of Railways, Posts &amp;
                                Telegraphs</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 13, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following the interview which I have had the honor to hold with his excellency, I
                    have the satisfaction of advising him that the producers of American oils were
                    permitted to take part in the public competition which took place on the 8th
                    instant for the furnishing of a quantity of 2,400,000 kilograms of mineral
                    lubricating oils.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Broqueville.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
